A||||5||Greg Piet||OIL FILTER !?!?!?!?||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||04-23-2001||03:06 PM||||In the 3.1 stroker topic there is reference to a motor getting hosed by using the wrong oil filter...   please someone elaborate on this...<P>I know that I have gotten 2 different size oil filters, one being about twice as long as the other...  is one better or worse for the car?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||04-23-2001||03:08 PM||||I just changed my oil (3.4) and used AC Delco PF52, works fine for me.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">    <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||04-23-2001||07:31 PM||||In my 87 GT it calls for the PF47, I however use the PF52 because it is larger.  I believe that in 88 was the only year recommended for the 52.  Something about the length of the filter in the earlier years, but I have plenty of room.  I was not able to find the internal relief bypass valve rating of the filter but I have not noticed a difference.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||04-23-2001||10:20 PM||||The oil filter problem was the main cause<BR>of the 84 4cyl problems. Pontiac originally<BR>specified an oil filter with no check valve<BR>which allowed all the oil from the filter to<BR>drain back into the pan. When started in the<BR>morning the car was dry and thus wore much<BR>quicker and then would usually throw a rod. <BR>The 47 and 52 are correct for the Fiero but<BR>the 52, as someone said above, holds more<BR>oil so it is the better of the two.<BR>Both have check valves.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||lou_dias||04-24-2001||09:48 AM||||Yes, the oil filter was part of a recall or technical ammendum as well.  My mechanic put in the PF47 into my 87GT and it ruined the bearings within 6000 miles.  Oil pressure is lower immediatley.  PF52 is the right oil filter for the Fiero V6 regardless of year.  The ammendum called for PF51 which was then discontinued and succeded by PF52.  It's the anti-drainback feature that helps the engine stay properly lubed.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_Freak||04-25-2001||12:13 AM||||I dropped in a relocator kit to avoid that oil on the block, starter and exhaust.  It' on the side of the cradle in front of the right wheel.  Works great.  I accually hold 6.5+Qts with the added hose and ph8 filter.  Also have the drainback valve.||||reg||1
